{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## COMPLETE ERROR-CODE INVENTORY (read-only audit, no code changed, no gate ops run)\n\n### Location correction\nThe workflow error vocabulary is NOT in `_engine/rebar_reconciler/_errors.py`, and there is **no `_workflow_caller_code` and no `invalid_input` code anywhere in the tree** (grep-confirmed). The real home is the top-level **`src/rebar/_errors.py`**: `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (15 codes) + `error_code_for()` (7 precedence branches). `_engine/rebar_reconciler/_errors.py` holds only reconciler *exception* classes (JiraAPIError, RetryExhaustedError, …), not error codes. 35ab's \"→ invalid_input\" is not present in the current tree.\n\n### Surface 1 — `error_code_for` + `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`)\n15 codes: ticket_not_found, store_uninitialized, show_failed, deps_failed, concurrency_conflict, claim_failed, invalid_ticket_type, tracker_root_unresolved, criterion_unknown_id, criterion_registry_malformed, criterion_missing_file, llm_unavailable, config_unreadable, config_insecure_url, command_failed.\nBranches:\n1. ConcurrencyError/ConcurrencyMismatch → concurrency_conflict — **accurate**\n2. TicketNotFoundError → ticket_not_found — **accurate**\n3. TrackerRootError → tracker_root_unresolved — **accurate**\n4a. InsecureUrlError → config_insecure_url — **accurate**; 4b. ConfigError → config_unreadable — **accurate** (mild lossy for malformed-but-readable; documented)\n5. `exc.error_code` passthrough → {invalid_ticket_type, store_uninitialized, ticket_not_found, claim_failed, show_failed, deps_failed, **pinned_ticket_read_failed**} — **accurate**, but `pinned_ticket_read_failed` ∉ KNOWN_ERROR_CODES → vocab-contract gap (child **0aee**, ready-to-fix).\n6. **`LLMError → llm_unavailable` — MISLEADING (ROOT DEFECT).** Accurate only for LLMUnavailableError/LLMConfigError. Misleading for: WorkflowError family (WorkflowParseError, WorkflowValidationError, WorkflowVersionError, ExpressionError), LLMInputRejectedError, RunawayToolLoopError, LLMBudgetExhaustedError, ContextWindowExceededError, StructuredOutputError, UnretryableOutputError, CompletionRecoveryError. (child **5f96** ready-to-fix for the runner subclasses; WorkflowError family stays with 73d8/551b.)\n7. fallback → command_failed — **lossy** (acceptable default).\n\n### Surface 2 — `_structured_llm_failure` (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:22`)\nHardcodes `error=\"llm_unavailable\"` for EVERY LLMError across the 4 MCP gate tools (review_code/scan_spec/verify_completion/review_plan). Carries truthful resolution_class/retryable/diagnostic alongside, but the top-level `error` string is the blanket misleading one. **MISLEADING, OBSERVABLE.** (child **fbc0**, escalate.)\n\n### Surface 3 — gate degrade verdicts (`llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`)\n`_degraded_plan_review_verdict` / `_degraded_code_review_verdict` / completion degrade set `coverage.llm_unavailable=True` on the `except (LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` arm — so an INPUT rejection is flagged as `llm_unavailable=True`. Boolean name overloaded to \"no provider record / degraded\". Consumers branch on it: drift_floor.py:202, orchestrator.py:468, review_bot/adapter.py:114. **MISLEADING NAME, OBSERVABLE.** (child **5f96**? no → dedicated child, escalate.)\n\n### Surface 4 — MCP envelope guard (`_mcp_errors.py::_envelope_error`)\nPure delegation to `error_code_for` (includes LLMError in the wrapped set). Inherits Surface-1 branch 6. The guard is installed BEFORE all tool registration (mcp_server.py:692 vs 704-706), so **`render_workflow` (read tool) → WorkflowParseError → llm_unavailable is OBSERVABLE today** (child **7d47**, escalate; the live manifestation of 551b/73d8).\n\n### Surface 5 — `ResolutionClass` taxonomy (`src/rebar/llm/failure.py`, `_map`/`_map_http`)\n8 classes (WAIT_AND_RETRY, RETRY_NOW, INCREASE_PROVIDER_LIMITS, CHANGE_SETTINGS, CHANGE_INPUT, CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL, FIX_AGENT_DESIGN, NEEDS_INVESTIGATION). These are remediation DISPOSITIONS, not cause-codes; reviewed each arm — largely **accurate** (429/5xx→WAIT_AND_RETRY, 402/insufficient_quota→INCREASE_PROVIDER_LIMITS, 401/403→CHANGE_SETTINGS, 413/ctx-400→CHANGE_INPUT, UsageLimit/IncompleteToolCall→FIX_AGENT_DESIGN, FallbackExceptionGroup→CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL). Notable:\n- [agents]-absent import failure (incl. a missing-extra LLMConfigError) → NEEDS_INVESTIGATION — **lossy** (CHANGE_SETTINGS derivable) but deliberate/guarded.\n- retryable-masking already owned by **1c0d** — referenced, NOT re-filed.\n- NEEDS_INVESTIGATION fallback — **lossy** by design.\nNo NEW misleading disposition found.\n\n### Surface 6 — `error_envelope` (`_engine_support/output.py`) — pure shape builder, no classification. N/A.\n### Surface 7 — reader CLI (`_engine_support/reads_cli.py`): show→show_failed (accurate); deps → `\"not found\" in message ? ticket_not_found : deps_failed` — **lossy/fragile string-sniff**, lands correctly; low risk, note-only.\n### Surface 8 — `explain_criterion` (`_mcp_reads.py:270`): unknown-id/malformed-registry/missing-file → specific codes (**accurate**); unknown kind → command_failed (**lossy** fallback, acceptable).\n### Surface 9 — exit codes: reconciler PassDisposition (RESCHEDULE=75, success=0) and gate exits (1 fail / 2 indeterminate / 10 concurrency / 11 retryable) — **accurate** process dispositions.\n\n### TALLIES\n- Distinct workflow vocabulary codes: **15** in KNOWN_ERROR_CODES + **1** emitted-but-unregistered (pinned_ticket_read_failed) = 16.\n- ResolutionClass dispositions: **8**.\n- Classification of the mappings reviewed: **accurate** — branches 1–5, ResolutionClass arms, exit codes, criterion/show mappings (the large majority). **MISLEADING** — the `LLMError → llm_unavailable` pattern at 3 sites: Surface 1 branch 6, Surface 2 (_structured_llm_failure), Surface 3 (coverage.llm_unavailable bool). **lossy** — command_failed, NEEDS_INVESTIGATION, config_unreadable(malformed), deps string-sniff, missing-extra→NEEDS_INVESTIGATION.\n- **Observable misleading:** 7d47 (render_workflow), fbc0 (_structured_llm_failure), + Surface 3 boolean (dedicated child).\n- **Latent misleading:** 5f96 (error_code_for branch 6 for runner subclasses — reachable but intercepted upstream today), 551b (editor WorkflowParseError, CLI-only), 73d8 (ExpressionError, execute-time run-state, not classifier).\n\n### Known instances folded in (not duplicated)\n- **551b** (missing-bundle WorkflowError, editor, latent/escalated) and **73d8** (ExpressionError, execute-time, escalate) are both instances of Surface-1 branch 6. 7d47 links to both as the OBSERVABLE MCP manifestation of the same branch.\n\n### Surface where accuracy could NOT be fully determined\n- Surface 5 `ModelAPIError → RETRY_NOW` and `HTTP 400-else → CHANGE_SETTINGS`: defensible but arguable; whether a generic non-HTTP `ModelAPIError` is truly retry-now vs needs-investigation depends on provider behavior not observable statically. Left as accurate-enough, flagged here rather than filed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788056735739715796,"uuid":"c00d6718-7197-4407-acf7-c535a1b1257e"}